jobResponsibilities:
Your main responsibilities will be to provide administrative support in ensuring efficient management of daily tasks and scheduling of engagements for your principal. The key responsibilities include:  

a. Scheduling of meetings/events/engagements.  
b. Managing calendars, emails and phone calls;  
c. Making official work trip arrangements;  
d. Administrative support for the principal, and for the Division as assigned; 
e. Assist in organising events and/or related support work for the department 
f. Maintaining records and filing systems;  
g. Taking minutes of meetings; 
h. Managing budgets and expenditure; and 
i. Any other duties assigned by your principal.

The Private & Shared Mobility Division oversees the development of private transport policies, encompassing vehicles, roads, and active mobility, and is also responsible for the development of strategies to prepare the MOT Family for future mobility challenges and opportunities, particularly in the areas of sustainability, research and development and inter-modal connectivity. 

As part of the Private Mobility team, you are expected to work together with other government agencies to:
• Develop and review private mobility strategies and policies, such as on the Certificate of Entitlement;
• Develop measures to contribute to the transport sector’s move towards sustainability, including measures to scale up electric vehicle adoption;
• Study trends that may impact the future of transport and develop proposals to enable Singapore to stay ahead of these trends; and
• Engage international and local thought leaders from both the private and public sectors, as well as help spur industry development efforts.

jobRequirements:
Write to us if you are/have:

1. Strong written and verbal communication skills;
2. Sound research, analytical, comprehension and decision-making abilities;
3. Meticulous, customer-oriented and attentive to detail;
4. An interest in, or have some understanding of, how businesses brand, market and identify themselves;
5. Able to work well both as a team player and as an individual contributor with a strong sense of ownership and responsibility for meeting personal targets and deadlines;
6. Adept at managing multiple tasks or projects concurrently;
7. Self-motivated, adaptable and keen to take on new challenges; and
8. Committed to continuous professional and personal development.

jobResponsibilities:
As the Deputy Director, you will lead a dynamic and dedicated team responsible for advancing 
Singapore’s economic engagement with the vibrant markets of Southeast Asia and Oceania. You will 
work on creative and innovative initiatives with colleagues in METI and our economic agencies that 
will develop your and your team’s international economic perspectives, capabilities and experience 
by:  

• Analysing and assessing geostrategic developments and trends that affect the flows of goods, 
services, and investments;  

• Formulating and reviewing strategies, policies and projects that enhance Singapore’s bilateral 
and plurilateral economic relations with Southeast Asia and Oceania, in consultation and 
coordination with other Government ministries and agencies; 

• Leading negotiations and discussions with international counterparts;  

• Networking and developing connections with foreign government and business 
representatives;  

• Fronting communications, consultations and engagements with key stakeholders in the 
business community and general public;  

• Organising and representing METI in visits, meetings, negotiations and conferences.

agencyDescription:
The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is responsible for managing Singapore’s fiscal policies and the structure of its economy. We work to maintain international standards and best practices in areas such as company law, accounting standards, and corporate governance principles. We aim to advance the well-being and development of Singapore by:

•	achieving a balanced budget through prudent and sustainable fiscal policies;
•	ensuring the prudent investment of the government's reserves and other public funds;
•	setting out policies for government procurement, customs regulation, accounting standards and business regulation;
•	fostering a regulatory environment conducive to business and enterprise; and
•	ensuring that businesses operating within Singapore's jurisdiction are compatible with international standards and practices, in areas such as company law, accounting standards and corporate governance principles.

jobResponsibilities:
Key results areas include:
• Drive KM initiatives such as digitisation of physical files, archival research, and knowledge and records audits;
• Develop and review KM policies, internal guidelines and training materials;
• Manage the physical and electronic records of the organisation over their lifecycle e.g. appraisal, archival and declassification, and liaise with National Archives of Singapore (NAS);
• Manage KM system projects, including requirements gathering, stakeholder and vendor coordination, system testing, implementation, and user onboarding, to deliver digital solutions that support KM; and
• Foster a strong knowledge management culture for the organisation, which includes engagement of MOF officers and communication of best practices.

jobRequirements:
• Background in Knowledge Management, Information Science, Information Systems, Business Administration, and/or IT will be advantageous;
• Preferably 2-3 years’ experience in implementing knowledge management initiatives;
• Good understanding of records management, archiving and information classification concepts and systems, and the implementation of digital solutions and technological tools e.g. Sharepoint;
• Self-driven and committed individual who is able to work independently and within teams; and
• Strong critical thinking, communication (both written and presentation) and project management skills.

jobResponsibilities:
Specifically, you will: 

•	Develop and implement integrated communication strategies and create content that support METI’s announcements and initiatives; 
•	Design appropriate messaging to achieve the desired outcome of impactful and effective communication; 
•	Proactively develop media outreach and engagement strategies to profile and communicate the Ministry’s work; 
•	Collaborate with and manage external partners and agencies on media outreach and engagement; and 
•	Provide comms and staffing support for METI political office holders, including event assessments, drafting talking points and social media post(s), and handle media facilitation.

jobRequirements:
•	Relevant field of study in Communications, Public Relations, Arts and Social Sciences or relevant discipline; 
•	Minimum 1 to 2 years of related work experience in media relations or journalism preferred; applicants with no experience may apply;
•	Demonstrated ability in developing and implementing sound communications strategies and strong media relations skills; 
•	Good project management and organisational skills in a fast-paced environment; 
•	Strong writing skills; 
•	Interest in public sector policy matters and economy related issues; 
•	Able to negotiate and collaborate effectively at an advanced level.

agencyDescription:
The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is responsible for managing Singapore’s fiscal policies and the structure of its economy. We work to maintain international standards and best practices in areas such as company law, accounting standards, and corporate governance principles. We aim to advance the well-being and development of Singapore by:

•	achieving a balanced budget through prudent and sustainable fiscal policies;
•	ensuring the prudent investment of the government's reserves and other public funds;
•	setting out policies for government procurement, customs regulation, accounting standards and business regulation;
•	fostering a regulatory environment conducive to business and enterprise; and
•	ensuring that businesses operating within Singapore's jurisdiction are compatible with international standards and practices, in areas such as company law, accounting standards and corporate governance principles.

The National Research Foundation (NRF) was set up on 1 January 2006 as a department under the Prime Minister's Office. It was set up to perform the following:

a) To provide secretariat support to the Research, Innovation and Enterprise Council (RIEC), chaired by the Senior Minister;

b) To coordinate the research of different agencies within the larger national framework in order to provide a coherent strategic overview and direction;

c) To develop policies and plans to implement the five strategic thrusts for the national R&D agenda; and

d) To implement national research, innovation and enterprise strategies approved by the RIEC, and to allocate funding to programmes that meet NRF's strategic objectives.

jobRequirements:
• Minimum a Diploma Holder in relevant discipline such as Accounting/Finance/Business;

• Proficient in MS Word, Excel, and PowerPoint;

• Minimum 2 years of related working experience in similar position is preferred;

• Knowledge of NFS@Gov system and data analytics tool is advantageous; and

• Possess good interpersonal, communication and organizational skills;

• Diligent with an eye for details; and

• Able to work both independently and as a team player.

o	Prior experience in policy and planning roles preferred;
o	[For Head-level position] Prior experience in policy supervisory roles preferred;
o	Intellectual curiosity, and clear logical and systems thinking;
o	Excellent writing skills to deliver analyses synthesising information from multiple domains, including data-driven outputs; 
o	Experience engaging multiple agencies and stakeholders, with skills to listen empathetically, sense dynamics, and persuade and negotiate across agencies and seniority levels to achieve desired outcomes; 
o	Ability to move between macro and micro perspectives;
o	Preferably an intuitive grasp of Singapore’s security imperatives;
o	Interest in current affairs;
o	Ability to work in a dynamic environment and pick up new skills/ domain knowledge if necessary; and
o	Proactive, articulate, purpose-driven, persistent.

We may refer you as a potential candidate for vacancies in other agencies we assessed you to be suitable for. 
By applying for this job, you are aware of, and are also giving NSCS consent for the cross referral. If you do not wish to be cross referred, please inform us via this link: https://go.gov.sg/candidateoptout.

