jobResponsibilities:
TIER officers in the US Division are part of a dynamic and dedicated team responsible for advancing Singapore’s economic engagement with the United States. You will work on creative and innovative initiatives with colleagues in METI and our economic agencies that will develop your international economic perspectives, capabilities and experience by: 

•	Analysing and reporting on geostrategic developments and trends that affect the flows of goods, services, and investments; 

•	Formulating and refining strategies, policies and plans that enhance Singapore’s bilateral and plurilateral economic relations with the United States, often in consultation and coordination with other ministries and agencies across the Whole-of-Government; 

•	Networking and developing connections with foreign government and business counterparts; 

•	Preparing and executing communications, consultations and engagements with key stakeholders in the business community and general public; 

•	Organising and representing METI in visits, meetings, negotiations and conferences.

jobRequirements:
• Keen interest in international economic affairs and negotiations; 
• Strong analytical and conceptual abilities, with an eye for detail; 
• Excellent written and oral communication skills; 
• Self-starter, versatile and adaptable to different environments; 
• Ability to work well in teams and engage people; 
• Ability to work in a fast-paced and dynamic environment; and  
• Willingness to travel frequently

jobResponsibilities:
As an ITD officer, you will be assigned to one of four specialised teams covering trade in goods, digital economy and services, investment, or multilateral trade policy. You will deepen your knowledge, skills and expertise on a myriad of international trade issues and apply them in the following areas:

• Developing and implementing Singapore’s foreign economic policy;
• Representing Singapore in bilateral/multilateral trade and investment negotiations;
• Participating in international meetings and conferences;
• Providing advice to the Singapore Government on trade policy matters;
• Collaborating with external stakeholders, such as Singapore-based companies, business chambers and the general public;
• Ensuring Singapore’s full and timely implementation of international trade obligations; and
• Analysing international developments and their potential implications on Singapore

jobRequirements:
We are looking for candidates who are:
• Trained in Economics, Law, Political Science, International Relations, Accounting,
Business or related disciplines is preferred, but not essential;
• Keen interest in international economic affairs and negotiation;
• Strong analytical and conceptual abilities, with an eye for detail;
• Excellent written and oral communication skills;
• Ability to work well in teams and in a fast-paced and dynamic environment; and 
• Willingness to travel frequently

jobResponsibilities:
As a TIER officer in the Trade Strategy and Security Division, you will be part of a dynamic team working on fast-moving pieces to help Singapore navigate changes in our geo-economic environment. You will have the opportunity to hone your strategic thinking skillset, policy acumen, and international orientation perspectives in both the economic and security domains, by:

• Assessing the impact and implications of geo-political developments on Singapore’s economic and security interests;
• Developing strategies, policies, options and responses to expand Singapore’s economic heft or relevance as well as strengthen Singapore’s economic resilience;
• Preparing and executing communications and engagement strategies with key public and private sector stakeholders;
• Organising and representing METI at various high-level inter-agency platforms related to economic, security, and geo-political portfolios; and
• Collaborating and networking with various internal and external stakeholders

jobRequirements:
We are looking for dedicated team players who thrive in a fast-paced environment with:

• Relevant field of study in International Relations, Political Science, Public Policy,
Economics, Business, Finance, Accounting or any related discipline;
• Keen interest in the geo-political environment, as well as economic and security issues;
• Experience in policy formulation and data analysis;
• Excellent analytical, writing, communication, and presentation skills; and
• Strong project management and stakeholder management skills.

We are looking for someone who is curious about global and regional developments, enjoys engaging diverse stakeholders, and is motivated by the opportunity to contribute to policies and partnerships that strengthen Singapore's future. The successful candidate should also be committed to mentoring and developing officers, and to foster an inclusive and supportive team environment.

Some useful qualities include:
• Keen interest in North East Asian economies and regional developments;
• Excellent analytical and communication skills;
• Effectively bilingual in written and spoken English and Mandarin;
• Experience in public policy, economic policy, international relations, trade policy, investment promotion, or related fields;
• Experience in leading teams and managing stakeholder relationships; 
• Willingness to travel

jobResponsibilities:
Brief description of Job Scope:

The First Responders Team in PSV attends to high-risk and cases require immediate response. Reporting to the Team Lead/Senior Manager, your role is to undertake crisis case management duties, immediate safety planning and intervention work for high-risk child abuse, domestic violence and vulnerable adults experiencing violence, abuse or neglect cases. You will also support in developing operational processes, policies, systems and training for the team and work closely with the professional partners to ensure an effective protection system for them.

Responsibilities:

As a First Responder, you will:
•	Carry out statutory functions under the Children and Young Person Act, Women’s Charter and Vulnerable Adults Act in the protection of child abuse, domestic violence and vulnerable adults cases such as conducting on-site response to emergency cases, issuance of Protector Power/ Emergency Order to ensure safety etc.  
•	Respond on-site to high-risk cases involving child abuse, domestic violence and vulnerable adults, conduct safety assessment and implement immediate safety planning to ensure their safety, during and after-office hours;
•	Collaborate closely with the professional partners to ensure coordinated case management for the safety of the children, domestic violence survivors, vulnerable adults and their families; 
•	Develop and implement operational processes and policies to guide the team’s operations;
•	Work closely with the planning team to identify key competencies and trainings for the team; and
•	Identify and engage key professionals to collaborate and build up interface to facilitate a smooth service delivery.

Responsibilities:

As a Manager (Team Lead) / Senior Manager, you will:
•	Supervise a team of case workers who will be responding to high-risk cases on-site that involves child abuse, domestic violence and vulnerable adults, conduct safety assessment and implement immediate safety planning to ensure their safety, during and after-office hours;
•	Provide management clearance for safety decisions of the child abuse, domestic violence survivors, vulnerable adults and their families;
•	Collaborate closely with the professional partners to ensure coordinated case management for the safety of the CYP, domestic violence survivors, vulnerable adults and their families; 
•	Develop and implement operational processes and policies to guide the team’s operations;
•	Work closely with the planning team to identify key competencies and implement trainings for the team; 
•	Identify and engage key professionals to collaborate and build up interface to facilitate a smooth service delivery; and
•	Oversee staff development to ensure professional capacity of the officers by identifying training needs.

In this role, you will:

•	Develop national and sectoral strategies to secure the resilience of Singapore’s supply chains for essential and critical goods and services, and to mitigate and withstand impact from external shocks; 

•	Analyse and synthesize findings on critical sector supply chains, challenges and needs;

•	Build the division’s collaboration network with key stakeholders across the Government, industry and academia; 

•	Strengthen supply chain intelligence and analysis capabilities.

