jobDescription:
The Municipal Services Office (MSO) was set up in Oct 2014 to improve the coordination, delivery and quality of municipal services by Government and Town Councils. These services include the upkeep and improvement of common areas in public and private estates, and the upgrading or provision of facilities and infrastructure.

The next bound of municipal service delivery involves:
i. ramping up of forward intelligence capabilities powered by AI-driven predictive analytics to enable foresight planning and support the development of pre-emptive operations;

ii. deploying AI-enhanced data focused tools (e.g. dashboards, regular data reports and AI-powered analytics tools) to increase the productivity of officers across the municipal sector and to support them in making data-driven policy decisions;

iii. humanising the digitalisation of government services (e.g. OneService Chatbot) for an optimised, resident-centric experience.

jobResponsibilities:
Responsibilities:

As a Legal Specialist of the ILCT, your work will include:

• Review and process cases in accordance with the applicable legal requirements, standard operating procedures and
policies;

• Perform initial case assessments and establish nexuses;

• Coordinate with domestic agencies and requesting countries to ensure the efficient disposal of cases;

• Draft legal documents and assist in the preparation of legal applications to Court;

• Proactively track and monitor timelines for cases. Send out reminders to relevant parties for response;

• Attend meetings and court proceedings and prepare written reports;

• Assist with taking notes of court proceedings. From time to time, assist in the conduct of trials and other judicial
proceedings;

• Develop and maintain ILCT’s Knowledge Management (KM) materials;

• Conduct substantive legal research;

• Assist with ad-hoc projects and events organised by Crime Division & AGC; and

• Perform any other tasks as assigned by supervisors and to work collaboratively with colleagues within the Crime division and across other legal divisions.

Other Accountabilities:

As a member of the Singapore Public Service, you will also be responsible for ensuring the proper handling of files and
documents according to established and approved procedures, including handling and sealing documents based on
classification.

You will also be responsible for ensuring that all work, whether ad hoc or routine, is completed on time and of high standard.

This is an operations role, where you will be involved in licensing and regulatory compliance. You will be involved in the following key areas:

•	Regulate Early Childhood Development Centres (“Centres”) in Singapore to ensure compliance with the Early Childhood Development Centres Act and Regulations;
•	Monitor Centres and ensure compliance;
