jobResponsibilities:
We are looking for a proactive and dynamic individual to join the Financial Governance Team (FGT). In this role, you will help to strengthen MSF’s financial governance, including grant governance, through policy development, compliance, data & analytics, and cross-agency coordination. 

To be a strong contributor, you will need to:
•	Understand governance and risk management concepts and requirements; 
•	Apply concepts to develop governance policies;
•	Partner MSF’s divisions in the management of grants in compliance with the Instruction Manual on Grants Governance and continuously improve policies, processes and systems to strengthen grant governance and enhance operational efficiency; 
•	Monitor and report on governance and compliance standards, including identifying trends and areas for improvement; and
•	Leverage on data, analytics and AI tools to raise governance standards.

The scope of governance and risk management will primarily relate to financial control and grant administration, and will extend to performance evaluation and cross-agency coordination.

Responsibilities:

You will be part of a team responsible for improving financial and grant governance standards in MSF through policies, capability building and data analytics. 

To do so, you will need to partner with MSF divisions and Company Limited by Guarantee (CLG)  entities to:
•	Review and develop governance frameworks, processes, and systems to meet specific targets and timelines; 
•	Validate MSF divisions’ compliance with governance standards; 
•	Utilize and deploy AI tools for better understanding of, and compliance with, governance requirements; 
•	Develop and raise financial governance competencies among MSF’s grant officers; and
•	Drive and support data analytics framework and processes to meet risk management, fraud detection, investigation, and other reporting requirements.

You will also be required to oversee and collaborate with MSF divisions to implement programme evaluation plans to improve accountability and ensure that programme objectives are achieved.

You will develop and implement strategies, policies, and projects to empower Singapore’s social service sector to have a greater positive impact. For example, you will:

• Govern and administer funding to the social service sector;
• Develop a strategy and implementation plan on how to incentivise and support greater impact measurement and evaluation in the social service sector;
• Develop a strategy and implementation plan on how to incentivise and support more intentional and outcome-oriented technology adoption within the social service sector;
• Evaluate the latest philanthropic giving and social impact investing models and trends, and develop ways for the social service sector to better leverage such systems; and/or
• Develop and maintain strategic partnerships with other social service stakeholders to develop the social service sector.
